1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:04,990
A PPTX file does not mean everything inside is editable.

2
00:00:04,990 --> 00:00:08,166
This tool checks the file structure.

3
00:00:08,166 --> 00:00:13,837
We will use two original demo slides.
All business figures are synthetic.

4
00:00:14,837 --> 00:00:16,792
Start with the image-only file.

5
00:00:16,792 --> 00:00:20,947
Both slides contain pictures, with no separate text objects.

6
00:00:20,947 --> 00:00:26,814
The file opens, but you cannot directly edit the titles inside those pictures.

7
00:00:27,814 --> 00:00:30,077
Now check the native-object version.

8
00:00:30,077 --> 00:00:37,116
Across two slides: 44 text-bearing objects,
18 structural shapes, and 3 connectors.

9
00:00:37,116 --> 00:00:41,139
Download this sample to try selecting and editing its objects.

10
00:00:42,139 --> 00:00:48,308
The mixed file has a picture on slide one and native objects on slide two.
Check each slide.

11
00:00:48,308 --> 00:00:54,478
More objects do not prove text accuracy.
Table and chart data need separate checks.

12
00:00:55,478 --> 00:01:02,566
For a rebuild, specify the pages
and which text and shapes must remain editable.

13
00:01:02,566 --> 00:01:08,710
This form creates a written brief only. It does not submit an order.

14
00:01:09,710 --> 00:01:12,544
You can save the structure report to your computer.

15
00:01:12,544 --> 00:01:16,323
The file you select is processed in the current browser.

16
00:01:16,323 --> 00:01:24,117
Finally, make an edit in your presentation app.
Save and reopen it to check the content and layout.
